# Plico (太初) — AI-Native Operating System Kernel

## Project
Rust (edition 2021). AI-native OS kernel. No human CLI/GUI. Semantic APIs only.
Inference-framework-agnostic: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

## Build & Test
```bash
cargo build                                    # build
EMBEDDING_BACKEND=stub LLM_BACKEND=stub cargo test --lib   # unit tests (~2s)
EMBEDDING_BACKEND=stub LLM_BACKEND=stub cargo test         # all tests
cargo clippy -- -D warnings                    # lint (zero warnings required)
cargo fmt --check                              # format check
```

## Code Style
- Files: `snake_case.rs`, one concept per file, < 300 lines
- Naming: `snake_case` fns, `PascalCase` types, `SCREAMING_SNAKE` consts
- No `#[allow(clippy::...)]` — fix the issue, don't suppress
- No `unsafe` without `# Safety` comment
- Errors: `thiserror` typed errors only, no panics in lib code
- Tests: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` inline in source files

## Architecture
- Dependency: `api/bin → kernel → tool/fs/intent → cas/memory/scheduler/temporal/llm`
- `kernel/` is the only module importing all others — all calls go through `AIKernel`
- CAS is the only module touching the host filesystem
- JSON is the only kernel interface format

## Testing Patterns
- Kernel tests: `crate::kernel::tests::make_kernel()` returns `(Arc<AIKernel>, TempDir)`
- Handler tests: `ApiRequest` → `kernel.handle_api_request(req)` → check `ApiResponse`
- Tool tests: `handle(kernel, "tool.name", &params, agent_id)` → check `ToolResult`
- Stub embedding returns empty vectors — don't assert search result counts

## Security
- Reserved agent names: `kernel`, `system`, `root`, `admin` — cannot be registered
- Max content: 10 MB per object
- All persistence uses `atomic_write_json()` — never `std::fs::write()` for JSON
- No hardcoded API keys — use env vars or `~/.plico/` config
